      <Comment source="BioCyc">Activituy of the maize protein is inferred from similarity to the Arabidopsis YUC2 protein, whcih was shown in a heterologous host, E. coli, to convert indole-3-pyruvate (IPA) to indole acetic acid, and without an indole acetaldehyde intermediate|CITS: [22025724]|. YUC2 enzyme assays were performed at 30 degrees C, pH7.4, with 100 micromolar IPA, 1 mmolar NADPH and 40 micromolar FAD. Kinetic parameters (Km, Vmax) were not determined.</Comment>
